🌟 Today, we're exploring Containers, Images, and Essential Commands—the building blocks of Docker mastery.

Container Management 📦 :
🔻 docker ps -a→ Lists all containers (running and stopped).
🔻docker images→ Displays all available images.
🔻docker stop (container_name) → Stops a running container.
🔻docker start (container_name)→ Starts a stopped container.
🔻docker rm (container_name)→ Removes a container (must be stopped first).
🔻docker ps -a -f status=exited→ Filters the list to show only exited containers.
🔻docker stop $(docker ps -q)→ Stops all running containers.
🔻docker start $(docker ps -a -q)→ Starts all stopped containers.
🔻docker rm -f (container_name)→ Forcefully removes a container (even if running).

Image Management 📼:
🔻docker run (image_name)→ Runs a container from an image.
🔻docker rmi (repository:tag)→ Removes an unused image.
🔻docker rm -f (container_ID)→ Forcefully removes a container by ID.
🔻docker inspect (container_name/ID)→ Shows detailed container information.


Docker file 🗃️:
It is a text based file which contains some set of instructions and it helps to automate the docker image creation.
There is no syntax for docker file

Important components in docker file ✍️:
1. FROM: Base image (e.g., `FROM ubuntu:20.04`). 
2. COPY: Copy the files from host (Local) to container.
3. ADD: Copy the files from host (Local) to container and also it will download the file from the internet and send those to the container.
4. RUN: Execute commands during image build (e.g., `RUN apt-get update`). 
5. CMD: Default command to run when the container starts. 
6. ENTRYPOINT: Configure a container to run as an executable. 
7. WORKDIR: Set working directory for subsequent instructions. 
8. ENV: Set environment variables (e.g., `ENV APP_PORT=8080`). 
9. ARG: Build-time variables (e.g., `ARG VERSION=1.0`). 
10. EXPOSE: Document the port the container listens on. 
11. USER: Switch user for security (e.g., `USER node`). 
12. LABEL: Add metadata (e.g., `LABEL maintainer="your@email.com"`). 
13. MAINTAINER : used to specify the author or maintainer of the image.
